{"ticker":"BHARATRAS","symbol":"BHARATRAS","instrumentId":3028605,"name":"Bharat Rasayan","industry":"NSE-Chemicals-Agricultural","about":"Bharat Rasayan Ltd. is a prominent agrochemical company in India, engaged in the manufacturing of technical grade pesticides, insecticides, herbicides, and fungicides. The company provides a wide range of crop protection products designed to enhance agricultural productivity and safeguard crops from pests and diseases. With state-of-the-art manufacturing facilities and a strong emphasis on research and development, Bharat Rasayan produces high-quality agrochemicals that meet international standards. It serves both domestic and global markets, supplying to farmers, distributors, and other agrochemical companies. Committed to sustainable agriculture, Bharat Rasayan focuses on innovation and environmental safety, contributing significantly to India’s agricultural growth.","website":"www.bharatgroup.co.in","location":"New Delhi, INDIA","exchange":"NSE","fetchedAt":"2026-11-20T13:08:54.427Z","basis":"consolidated","price":{"value":928,"changePct":-90.62626262626262,"week52High":2625,"week52Low":914.55},"stats":[{"label":"Market capitalization","value":"₹1,542 Cr"},{"label":"Sales","value":"₹1,269 Cr"},{"label":"Shares in float","value":"1,038,000"},{"label":"No. of funds","value":"35"},{"label":"Shares held by funds","value":"379,889"},{"label":"Dividend yield","value":"0.03%"},{"label":"Book value","value":"1.21"},{"label":"U/D vol ratio","value":"0.9"},{"label":"LTDebt / equity","value":"—"},{"label":"Alpha","value":"-2.02"},{"label":"Beta","value":"0.26"},{"label":"EPS growth rate","value":"-15%"},{"label":"P/E ratio","value":"11.28"},{"label":"5-year P/E range","value":"10–68"},{"label":"Return on equity","value":"11.4%"},{"label":"Cash flow (INR)","value":"413.97"},{"label":"Volume","value":"13,370"},{"label":"Avg volume (50d)","value":"18,372"},{"label":"Master score","value":"32"},{"label":"EPS rating","value":"42"},{"label":"P